{% extends "layout/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="dest-page-hero" id="top">

  <div class="dest-page-hero__img">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/images/photos/alaska-glacier-hero.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
      <img
        class="dest-page-hero__photo"
        src="/images/photos/alaska-glacier-hero.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
        alt="Chuck and his wife on an Alaska glacier during a Royal Caribbean cruise"
        width="2400"
        height="1350"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
    </picture>
  </div>
  <div class="dest-page-hero__overlay"></div>

  <nav class="dest-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <div class="dest-breadcrumb__inner">
      <a href="/" class="dest-breadcrumb__link">Home</a>
      <span class="dest-breadcrumb__sep">&rsaquo;</span>
      <span class="dest-breadcrumb__current">Royal Caribbean</span>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="dest-page-hero__content">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Royal Caribbean</p>
    <h1 class="dest-page-hero__headline">
      The world's greatest<br>
      cruise line, from someone<br>
      who's <em>sailed it.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="dest-page-hero__sub">
      Caribbean islands, Alaskan glaciers, Bermuda — I've sailed Royal Caribbean in interior cabins and on the balcony, with young kids, with teenagers, and as a couple. My recommendations come from being there.
    </p>
    <a href="{{ site.links.consultation }}" class="btn btn--gold">
      Start Your Escape
    </a>
  </div>

</section>

<!-- Intro -->
<section class="dest-intro">
  <div class="dest-intro__inner">
    <p class="dest-intro__lead">
      Royal Caribbean is the cruise line I recommend most often — not because it's the only option, but because I've seen it work for first-timers, families with kids, multigenerational groups, and couples who want something more adventurous.
    </p>
    <p class="dest-intro__body">
      My 5th and 6th Royal Caribbean sailings are booked for July and August 2026. I've also cruised Norwegian and Disney Cruise Line. I keep returning to Royal for the ship experiences, the variety of itineraries, and the way the product genuinely works for every age in the group.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Personal Story -->
<section class="dest-story" id="our-experience">
  <div class="dest-story__inner">

    <div class="dest-story__text">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Our Experience</p>
      <h2 class="dest-story__headline">
        Three oceans.<br>
        Every kind of <em>traveler.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        Royal Caribbean is the cruise line I recommend to first-timers because the ships have something for everyone and the value is genuinely hard to beat. I've sailed the Caribbean with young kids, navigated Alaska with teenagers, and explored Bermuda as a couple. Each trip taught me something different about how to make the most of it.
      </p>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        The Alaska glacier excursion in the photo — that's my wife and me on a real Royal Caribbean itinerary. Trips like that are why I take ship and cabin selection seriously. The right itinerary on the wrong ship, or the wrong stateroom for how your family actually travels, can change the whole experience.
      </p>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        On Oasis of the Seas we've done the big-ship energy right: family dinners, snorkeling, and the kind of sea days that end up being everyone's favorite once you're on board. I plan those details the same way I planned complex systems in corporate IT — with precision, but never at the expense of the trip feeling easy.
      </p>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        Whether you're booking your first cruise, a milestone family sailing, or something more ambitious, I'll match you to the ship, itinerary, and cabin that fit your travelers — not just the fare that looks cheapest on the calendar.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="dest-story__photo">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/images/photos/alaska-glacier-story.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
        <img
          src="/images/photos/alaska-glacier-story.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
          alt="Chuck and his wife on an Alaska glacier during a Royal Caribbean cruise"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1600"
          height="1200"
        >
      </picture>
      <figcaption class="dest-story__caption">Alaska with my wife — Royal Caribbean</figcaption>
    </figure>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- Why Royal -->
<section class="dest-detail">
  <div class="dest-detail__inner">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Why Royal Caribbean</p>
    <h2 class="dest-detail__headline">
      What I help you <em>get right.</em>
    </h2>
    <div class="dest-detail__grid">
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">Ship &amp; itinerary fit</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          Wonder of the Seas in the Mediterranean is not the same product as Anthem in the Bahamas. I'll steer you toward the right class of ship for your ports, pace, and who's traveling.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">Cabin category</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          Interior, ocean view, balcony, or suite — the best choice depends on how you use the cabin. On Caribbean port-heavy weeks, an interior can be smart money; Alaska and sea-day-heavy trips often justify more space.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">Excursions &amp; sea days</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          I know when third-party excursions are worth the savings, when to book through the line, and how to structure sea days so the ship feels like a destination — not downtime you're enduring.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">Packages &amp; add-ons</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          Beverage packages, specialty dining, Wi‑Fi — we'll run the math honestly for your group so you're not buying bundles that never pay off.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Insider Tips -->
<section class="dest-tips" id="tips">
  <div class="dest-tips__inner">

    <div class="dest-tips__header">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">What I've Learned</p>
      <h2 class="dest-tips__headline">
        Insider tips from<br>
        someone who's <em>sailed it.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="dest-tips__intro">
        Practical notes from real sailings — the kind of detail that doesn't show up in a brochure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dest-tips__grid">

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">01</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Interior Cabins Are Not a Compromise</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">In the Caribbean, you're off the ship from 8am to 6pm every port day. The cabin is for sleeping. Save the money for excursions and specialty dining — that's where the real memories are made.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">02</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">The Dining Package Math Rarely Works Out</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Specialty restaurants are genuinely great, but the main dining room is better than you'd expect. Buy one or two specialty dinners à la carte rather than committing to a package — you'll likely spend less and enjoy it more.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">03</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Book Excursions Early — the Right Ones</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Third-party excursions can run 40–60% cheaper than ship-booked ones for the same experience. I know which operators are reliable at which ports, and which ship excursions are worth the premium for the peace of mind.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">04</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Sea Days Are the Hidden Gem</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">First-timers often dread sea days. They end up being everyone's favorite. The ship comes alive, crowds thin at the pools by mid-morning, and it's the most genuinely relaxing day of the entire trip.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">05</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Run the Beverage Package Math Honestly</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">The package breaks even at roughly five to six drinks per person per day. Do the math for your family before buying it. If you're not drinkers, skip it. If you are, it's usually worth it — especially in Alaska where you're indoors more.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">06</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Ship Selection Matters as Much as Itinerary</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Wonder of the Seas in the Mediterranean is a fundamentally different experience than Anthem of the Seas in the Bahamas. I'll match you to the right ship for your family's priorities — not just the cheapest fare on the right dates.</p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Gallery -->
<section class="dest-gallery" id="gallery">
  <div class="dest-gallery__inner">

    <div class="dest-gallery__header">
      <h2 class="dest-gallery__headline">On board &amp; ashore</h2>
      <p class="dest-gallery__note">Family moments from our Royal Caribbean sailings</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dest-gallery__grid dest-gallery__grid--duo">
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/images/photos/oasis-dining-family-story.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
          <img
            src="/images/photos/oasis-dining-family-story.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
            alt="Family dining on Oasis of the Seas"
            loading="lazy"
            width="1600"
            height="1200"
          >
        </picture>
      </figure>
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/images/photos/oasis-snorkel-story.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
          <img
            src="/images/photos/oasis-snorkel-story.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
            alt="Snorkeling during a Royal Caribbean cruise"
            loading="lazy"
            width="1600"
            height="1200"
          >
        </picture>
      </figure>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{% include "partials/cta-strip.njk" %}

{% endblock %}